{%- comment -%}
  First-credit nudge: push body and email headline. Used by both Canvases in 02.

  Cases:
    1. Reward unused + a saved restaurant found in the Catalog -> name the restaurant
    2. Reward unused + restaurant ID missing from the Catalog, or
       no restaurant ID at all          -> Connected Content call for three nearby picks
    3. Case 2 + the call fails          -> generic copy, still sends
    4. No unused reward, or its minimum is missing -> abort the send

  Notes:
  - {%- -%} whitespace control keeps tag lines from adding blank lines to the push.
  - The reward is checked for presence before it's compared, because comparing a
    missing value to 0 can error in Liquid; abort_message stops rendering at once.
  - The copy always states the minimum. Without it the message would promise $25 off
    any meal, so a missing minimum aborts instead of sending.
  - first_reward_display is a preformatted string ("25", "12.50") synced from the
    warehouse; the raw amount is the fallback if it's missing.
  - The restaurant comes from the restaurant_saved event that started the Canvas
    (Canvas context), so the message names the place the user just saved.
    The first ID in saved_restaurants is the fallback.
  - The restaurants Catalog supplies the current name; an unknown ID returns an
    empty items array, so the size is checked before the name is used.
  - The Connected Content call only runs in case 2: every send from the browsing
    Canvas, and only fallback sends from the save Canvas. The endpoint is a
    placeholder for a recommendations service.
  - This copy is shared by push and email. liquid/ splits it into Content Blocks and
    builds the HTML email; a test checks that its push copy matches this file.
  - Attribute, Catalog, and field names are illustrative and to be mapped to inKind's schema.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- assign reward = custom_attribute.${first_reward_amount} -%}
{%- assign reward_display = custom_attribute.${first_reward_display} | default: reward -%}
{%- assign min_spend = custom_attribute.${first_reward_min_spend} -%}
{%- assign first_saved = custom_attribute.${saved_restaurants} | first -%}
{%- assign saved_id = context.${restaurant_id} | default: first_saved -%}

{%- unless reward -%}
  {%- abort_message("no unused reward") -%}
{%- endunless -%}
{%- if reward <= 0 -%}
  {%- abort_message("reward amount is zero") -%}
{%- endif -%}
{%- unless min_spend -%}
  {%- abort_message("reward minimum missing") -%}
{%- endunless -%}
{%- capture offer -%}${{ reward_display }} toward a ${{ min_spend }}+ meal{%- endcapture -%}

{%- if saved_id -%}
  {% catalog_items restaurants {{ saved_id }} %}
  {%- if items.size > 0 -%}
    {%- assign saved_name = items[0].name -%}
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endif -%}

{%- if saved_name -%}
Your {{ offer }} is waiting at {{ saved_name }}. Dinner tonight?
{%- else -%}
  {%- connected_content https://api.example.com/v1/recommendations/nearby?user_id={{ ${user_id} | url_encode }}&limit=3 :save recs :cache_max_age 900 :retry -%}
  {%- if recs.__http_status_code__ != 200 or recs.restaurants.size == 0 -%}
Your {{ offer }} is waiting. Find a spot near you tonight.
  {%- else -%}
Your {{ offer }} is waiting. Nearby: {{ recs.restaurants | map: 'name' | join: ', ' | truncate: 80 }}
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endif -%}
